"""Frontier-driven session loop and centralized scheduler state.

``MiniSession`` owns the problem, dossier, proof state, conversation, budgets,
stagnation tracking, and recorder normalization. Actions declare their state
writes and return typed outcomes through ``apply``. Selection prefers proof
frontier work and uses static priority only for eligible work without a frontier
representation; recursive work executes inside bounded child sessions.
"""

